Hi Alex,

Following up on your question about the existing conveyor and sortation line at
Riverside.

- The conveyor and sortation equipment was installed in 2011 by a supplier that no
  longer exists, and nobody on our side has opened its control cabinet in years.
  It's old enough, and been patched enough times by different contractors over
  the years, that we genuinely don't know what's in there any more.
- We'd like your system to drive diverts on this conveyor for the new
  goods-to-person zone rather than replace it, since replacing it isn't in this
  phase's budget.
- Even once your engineers get hands-on with the cabinet, we'd expect how much
  rework your team finds to vary a lot: on a straightforward day it might just be
  a single modern PLC talking a standard protocol; on a bad day it might turn out
  to be two or three generations of patched-together controls with custom relay
  logic that takes far more effort to interface with safely. Nobody, including us,
  will know which it is until your team is actually in there working on it.
- So this isn't really something we can answer for you in advance — we'd expect
  your price to carry some built-in allowance for that uncertainty rather than
  assume the easy case.

Let us know if you need anything else from us before you price this.

Regards,
Priya Raman
